                <pb facs="0282" n="182" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg182"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.6363/721: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Robert Murray to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >New York</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-09-05"><hi rendition="#italic">September 5,
                        1920</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received September 6—6:50 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Roberto V. Pesqueira, general financial agent of the Mexican Government, is
                    desirous of talking with you informally and unofficially with particular
                    reference to the petroleum controversy which he is earnestly endeavoring to
                    arrange by direct negotiation with the heads of the companies. Will it be
                    possible for you to receive him on Wednesday or Thursday as he only awaits this
                    interview to return to Mexico to confer with the President. My address the City
                    Club.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Murray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
